 "notes": {
  "band-holds": "a fiber standing at the close of a band cannot leave while a child is alive, whatever mark has reached it",
  "band-own-mark": "the band's own mark is what the close was for, so nothing leaves when there is nothing to report",
  "band-restamp": "the mark that stood when the fiber first tried to leave the band is not the mark it leaves under: the child raises a new one while it waits",
  "band-snag": "a fiber unwinding into a band it owns marks the band's own guard, so the children stop instead of running on under an exception already in flight",
  "bundle-order": "collected payloads leave in the order the children ended, which is not the order they were made",
  "cleanup-outside": "a cleanup block runs after its own guard has closed, so its checkpoints answer to the enclosing chain and not to the guard it belongs to",
  "cleanup-raises": "an exception raised inside a cleanup block replaces the one already travelling, rather than being dropped for it",
  "cleanup-shielded": "MUST-WORK: shielding the enclosing guard from inside the cleanup block lets the block finish under an outer mark",
  "cleanup-under-outer-mark": "the same cleanup block with the enclosing guard marked: the block is abandoned at its first checkpoint",
  "cross-fiber-mark": "a child marking a guard of its parent reaches the parent while it sleeps",
  "deadline-at-entry": "a guard whose deadline has already passed when it is opened is marked there and then, not at the next advance of the clock",
  "deadline-elsewhere": "MUST-WORK: a deadline on a guard the fiber is not inside leaves it alone",
  "deadline-wakes-sleeper": "a deadline landing on a sleeping fiber wakes it at the deadline rather than at the end of its wait",
  "err-passes-guards": "an error is not a cut: no guard takes it, marked or not",
  "mark-twice": "MUST-WORK: marking a guard that is already marked changes nothing and does not report a second time",
  "nested-band": "a bundle leaving an inner band is collected by the outer one and leaves again with the payloads it carried",
  "no-mark-no-cut": "MUST-WORK: nothing marked, every block runs and the fiber ends ok",
  "outer-outranks-bundle": "a mark on a guard enclosing the band outranks what the children collected, and the cut leaves on its own",
  "outer-wins": "delivery goes to the outermost marked guard, not the innermost: attributing inward lets the fiber emit a token inside a guard already marked",
  "outer-wins-deep": "same, three deep, with the middle guard also marked",
  "shield-drop": "dropping the shield puts the outer mark back in view at the next checkpoint, because marks are sticky rather than consumed",
  "shield-hides-outer": "MUST-WORK: the fiber runs to the end of the shielded region with an outer guard marked the whole time",
  "shield-owns-mark": "a shield hides the marks outside its guard, never the mark on that guard itself",
  "shielded-child-survives": "MUST-WORK: a child shielded from the band's mark runs to its own end and its tokens stand",
  "spawn-inherits-band": "MUST-WORK: a child answers to the chain that stood when the band was opened, not to the guards its parent opened afterwards",
  "stale-stamp": "the guard a cut was raised for is not the guard it comes to rest at: a sibling marks an enclosing guard while the fiber is parked at a band it cannot leave, and no checkpoint stands between that mark and the boundary",
  "unmarked-guard-passes-it": "only a marked guard takes a cut: the band's own guard is marked and popped without absorbing it, so the cut reaches an unmarked enclosing guard with nothing visible marked, goes straight through, and leaves with the fiber",
  "zero-wait": "a wait of zero is still a checkpoint"
 }
}
